                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_06\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes XReservation.java's constructor/init switch statement so that the Group, Curriculum, and Course cases each read their own type-specific ApplicationProperty settings (ReservationPriorityGroup/Curriculum/Course, ReservationCanOverLimitGroup/Curriculum/Course, ReservationMustBeUsedGroup/Curriculum/Course, ReservationAllowOverlapGroup/Curriculum/Course) instead of incorrectly reusing the \"Individual\" properties.\n\ncandidate_06's diff (around lines 393-424) shows this exact switch statement being newly added (all lines prefixed with `+`, i.e., this code did not exist before this commit). In that newly-introduced code, the Group, Curriculum, and Course cases all call setPriority/setCanAssignOverLimit/setMustBeUsed/setAllowOverlap using the ReservationPriorityIndividual/ReservationCanOverLimitIndividual/ReservationMustBeUsedIndividual/ReservationAllowOverlapIndividual properties \u2014 the identical copy-paste bug described in the fix commit message (\"fixed an issue taking all the properties ... from individual reservation\").\n\nSince this switch statement (and the bug pattern) is created for the first time in candidate_06, and no earlier candidate contains this code, candidate_06 is the commit that introduced the bug. Later candidates (e.g., candidate_08) simply retain/inherit this buggy code until the fix commit corrects it.\n"
